{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bold-abeyant-indri","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nTwenty-seven bugs in the fortnight defect review were tests that could not fail or that burned CI time: subprocess oracles asserting only that a string is absent with no return-code check (`obvious-saline-gerbil`, `sound-bumpkinly-thrush`), a test burning the full 120 s Jira readiness budget per xdist worker (`albinic-kyanite-goldeneye`), wall-clock oracles (`tapestried-abhorrent-tuna`). The project already runs `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py` and pins `pytest-timeout==2.4.0`, but the budget is set only on the CI command line (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:656-672`, `--timeout=300`), so local runs have none, and Ruff does not select `PLW1510` (subprocess.run without `check=`) or the `PT` flake8-pytest-style family. Operator decision (2026-08-21): adopt only what is common practice in maintained OSS projects; a 20-second per-test budget is approved with an explicit override for tests that must be slow.\n\n## Approach\nStandard tooling only, no custom linter: (1) add `PLW1510` and `PT` to `[tool.ruff.lint] select` in `pyproject.toml`, clearing the existing backlog in the same change (PT findings that are stylistic go in `ignore` with a comment, not per-line `noqa`); (2) move the per-test budget into `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`: `timeout = 20`, `timeout_method = \"thread\"`, `timeout_func_only = true`, and drop `--timeout=300` from the CI invocation so the ini value applies; (3) the override is `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` on tests that must be slow, each carrying a one-line comment naming why; (4) add `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` and `check_raw_git_writes.py` to `make lint` (the pattern task `aciduric-enhanced-piranha` establishes). Not adopted because no maintained tool does it: lints for subprocess `timeout=`, `sleep` budgets, `os.environ.copy()`, `sys.modules` writes, foreign `.git/` writes; the `xdist_group` case is already covered by `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py`.\n\n## Scope\n`pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, `tests/**` (backlog fixes for PLW1510/PT and `timeout` marks on slow tests), `docs/local-dev-env.md` (document the override).\n\n## Testing\nMechanical plus one behavioural check: a deliberately sleeping 25 s test fails under the ini budget and passes with the marker. Pinning: the full default tier passes under `-n 4` with the new budget; `make lint` is green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `ruff check` with `PLW1510` and `PT` selected reports zero findings on `main`; checked by `make lint`.\n- [ ] A test exceeding 20 s without the marker fails locally and in CI; a marked test passes; checked by the two-test probe (removed before landing or kept under `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` with the slow one marked).\n- [ ] `make lint` runs the wall-clock and raw-git checks; checked by `make -n lint`.\n","id":"73b8-2d79-3046-44ce","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Adopt standard test-hygiene tooling: ruff PLW1510 + PT, pytest-timeout 20 s budget with marker override, hygiene checks in make lint"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787354731920556001,"uuid":"78611ccc-e1fb-4861-b05b-644d4339a680"}